The guest image aggregates software under several licenses.

  Component      Version    License        Build recipe and configuration
  ------------   --------   ------------   ------------------------------
  Linux          6.18.55    GPL-2.0-only   image/kernel/
  BusyBox        1.38.0     GPL-2.0-only   image/init/
  ONNX Runtime   1.31.1     MIT            image/onnxruntime/

Linux and BusyBox are not modified; the recipes above pin upstream sources by
digest and select which parts are built. They also satisfy GPL-2.0 section 3.

ONNX Runtime is built from its upstream source, with the patches its own build
applies, and linked into the process the execution worker runs a model in. Its
build takes third-party sources, each pinned by digest in its recipe: abseil,
flatbuffers and onnx (Apache-2.0), protobuf, re2 and cpuinfo (BSD), date,
nlohmann json, GSL and SafeInt (MIT), Boost.Mp11 (BSL-1.0) and Eigen
(MPL-2.0).

Enclavid's own components are Apache-2.0 — see ../LICENSE.
